    'female|a||Across: the share of the newly covered who are the eager kind, who would sign up on their own. Up: good days added per person.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1wkzmes'
    'female|a||If everyone covered is eager, the average gain is the ATT from our town: six days.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1lx282o'
    'female|a||If everyone covered is reluctant, it''s the ATU: one day.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:euueso'
    'female|a||Every mix in between sits on the straight line joining them: the same weighted average, now as a picture.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:uyw1y4'
    'female|a||Our whole town, forty percent eager, lands at three: the ATE.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:df8bkd'
    female|a||Now borrow Oregon's design. In 2008 the state had money for about ten thousand more Medicaid places, and about ninety thousand people put their names down for a lottery.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:pcz5xk'
    female|a||Only people who signed up could be drawn, and in our town those are the eager forty.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:tb6axz'
    female|a||Winners and losers come from that same pool, so the draw makes them alike, and the comparison is internally valid.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1qanucg'
    female|a||Run in our town, it would report six days, and six is exactly right, for the volunteers.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:19tjb7'
    'female|a||In the real Oregon, only about a quarter more of the winners than the losers ended up covered. So its estimate speaks for a narrower group still: the people the draw itself moved into coverage.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:8b62gb'
    female|a||A new state. A neighbouring state will cover all its uninsured, and four in five of them are the reluctant kind. About how many good days per person should it expect?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:yz73ld'
    'female|a||About two: one fifth eager and four fifths reluctant puts it a fifth of the way along the line, at two days.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9080
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||At one fifth eager the line gives two days: a third of what the lottery found, with the same insurance and the same kinds of people.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9280
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Watch the point slide along the line as the mix changes, and the gain per person with it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1ci4nl'
    female|a||It climbs from one day toward six as the mix gets more eager. The lottery's six holds only at the far right, where everyone is eager.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9800
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Nothing was wrong with the lottery. Its estimate is right for the people the draw moved into coverage; the next state simply covers different people.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:eitf4q'
    female|a||And this line assumes each kind gains the same everywhere. A sicker state, or one with fewer doctors, would move the line itself.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:4ai2he'
    female|a||Is this only a toy? Two real reforms suggest it isn't.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1o6xt73'
    female|a||In Oregon, coverage sent people to the emergency room more often, not less.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5600
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||Taubman and colleagues, in Science in 2014, read Portland-area emergency-room records: about eighteen months on, coverage added about four tenths of a visit a person, some forty percent, give or take a quarter of a visit.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 15080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1m6hmft'
    female|a||In Massachusetts, after its 2006 reform pushed coverage close to universal, emergency visits fell, or held steady.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:79za13'
    female|a||One result came from a lottery, the other from a reform with no coin, so it was tempting to trust Oregon alone.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1t3ugdf'
    female|a||The economist Amanda Kowalski asked whether the two were even measuring the same people's effect.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:15ubl3i'
    'female|a||Line people up by how readily they take up coverage: the most eager on the left, the most reluctant on the right.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1wglof2'
    'female|a||The people Oregon''s lottery moved sit toward the left: in her sample, fifteen percent of the losers and forty-one percent of the winners were covered.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1905gqu'
    female|a||And they were a little more likely to have used the emergency room before than those who stayed out even when drawn.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:gcmpqx'
    'female|a||Under her assumptions, the effect falls from left to right: positive for the people the lottery moved, below zero for the reluctant.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:qbkvrw'
    female|a||Massachusetts started with about nine in ten already insured and moved to about ninety-four, so the people it added were the last, healthier holdouts.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:gfddon'
    'female|a||On her line they sit where the effect is below zero: visits could fall there and rise in Oregon, with both studies right.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:q19jl'
    female|a||And reweighting Oregon by age, income, or anything else we can measure does not close the gap. The difference runs along eagerness itself.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:169t7lj'
    female|a||Not everyone is convinced. Her line assumes the effect changes in a straight line, and in her own sample, people who entered the lottery alone, Oregon's estimate is only about a quarter of a visit, and not statistically significant.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 15200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1al38r5'
    female|a||She notes that Massachusetts added higher-income people, many enrolling to avoid a penalty. Sceptics say such differences, or differences in the supply of care, could explain the gap on their own.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1y76m32'
    female|a||A lottery that also reached the reluctant would tell these readings apart.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1ges1il'
    female|a||One new case. A job-training scheme was tested by lottery among unemployed people who applied for it, because they expected it to help. Now it becomes compulsory for everyone unemployed. Per person, what should the government expect?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 14840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ql4jx'
    'female|a||Smaller: the applicants chose it because they expected to gain; compulsion adds the people who did not, so the trial''s fair estimate belongs to a different group.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11160
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||So an average effect is never just the effect of a treatment. It belongs to a population.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||The effect on the treated and the effect on everyone part when gains differ and people choose by them.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1cmbhyx'
    female|a||And a perfectly fair experiment is right for the people it moved, and silent about the rest.:
